From: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] stdafx.h: include stdint.h when config.h is not available

stdafx.h guards its <stdint.h> include on HAVE_STDINT_H, which comes from
libmodplug's own config.h - a build-time header that is not installed. An
external consumer therefore gets neither the guard's value nor the include,
and reaches the typedefs below with no uint8_t in scope:

  stdafx.h:78:9: error: 'uint8_t' does not name a type
     78 | typedef uint8_t UCHAR;

which then surfaces further along as every BYTE, WORD and DWORD in
sndfile.h failing to name a type. Both headers are installed and are the
documented way to reach CSoundFile, so this makes them unusable outside
the source tree - solarus includes exactly these two and cannot build.

stdint.h is C99 and C++11; there is no target here that installs this
header and lacks it.

Upstream: https://github.com/Konstanty/libmodplug/issues
Signed-off-by: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>

--- a/src/libmodplug/stdafx.h
+++ b/src/libmodplug/stdafx.h
@@ -19,6 +19,12 @@
 #endif
 #ifdef HAVE_STDINT_H
 # include <stdint.h>
+#else
+/* HAVE_STDINT_H comes from config.h, which is not installed alongside this
+ * header. Anything including it from outside the tree therefore reaches the
+ * typedefs below with no uint8_t in scope. stdint.h is C99 and C++11, so
+ * include it rather than leave the installed header unusable. */
+# include <stdint.h>
 #endif
 
 /* disable AGC and FILESAVE for all targets for uniformity. */
